    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 2, "2026-11-11 opus seed lane: status stays open. Re-verified on origin/release/1.0.0: rt_string_parse_int (runtime/src/value/collections.rs:6396) returns NIL/bare tagged int; primitive T? is by design a raw untagged payload-or-NIL-sentinel (runtime/src/value/sffi/io_print.rs rt_opt_i64_to_string doc; codegen/instr/mod.rs nil_tainted). Making parse_* yield Option::Some/None needs the seed-wide primitive-optional representation change (MIR lowering, HIR payload_slot_expr/lower_coalesce, cranelift+llvm call sites in codegen/instr/calls.rs, closures_structs.rs, llvm/functions*.rs) — not a single-site lane fix; partial change would desync the nil_tainted renderer. Seed is bootstrap-only; no spec or code landed. Direction decided by owner 2026-11-06 (seed .? = pure Simple parity): parse_* must return real Option Some/None on JIT/native matching interpreter; plan = seed-wide change across cranelift+llvm call sites, HIR/MIR lowering, nil print path, in a dedicated lane."

